Drop the vendor RAID CLIs here before running ./build.sh
=======================================================

Preferred layout (per architecture):

    vendor/cli/amd64/   storcli64, perccli, arcconf, ssacli, hpssacli
    vendor/cli/arm64/   storcli64, arcconf, hiraidadm
                        (ssacli/perccli have no arm64 build)

build.sh copies only the directory matching the target architecture into
config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/ at staging time.  Dropping binaries
straight into config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/ still works for amd64
(legacy layout); an arm64 build refuses x86 ELF files there.

The binaries are distributed by the vendors and CANNOT be shipped inside this
repository.  Put the decompressed ELF binaries straight into the directory
(no wrapper scripts, no directory named like the tool):

    storcli / storcli64     LSI / Broadcom MegaRAID
    perccli / perccli64     Dell PERC (same CLI grammar as storcli)
    arcconf                 Microchip / Adaptec SmartRAID
    ssacli / hpssacli       HPE Smart Array
    hiraidadm               Huawei HiRAID (aarch64 only; needs the hiraid driver)

Where they come from:

  storcli     Broadcom (or your OEM's support page) -> "storcli - MR7.x" ->
              storcli_all_os/Linux/storcli (or storcli64).
              Rename to `storcli` (or keep `storcli64`), chmod 755, drop it here.

  perccli     Dell support -> "Dell EMC PERC Command Line Interface" ->
              perccli / perccli64.  Keep the vendor binary name.

  arcconf     Microchip / Adaptec -> "ARCCONF Command Line Utility" ->
              arcconf_v3.*_linux_x64.tar.gz or the zip that contains the
              cmdline/arcconf binary. Rename to `arcconf`, chmod 755.

  ssacli      HPE Support Center -> "Smart Storage Administrator CLI" ->
              ssacli-*.x86_64.rpm works too:
                  rpm2cpio ssacli-*.rpm | cpio -idmv
                  cp usr/sbin/ssacli .../config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/
              or use the .deb variant with dpkg-deb -x.  Legacy hpssacli works.

Verification before building:

    for t in storcli storcli64 perccli perccli64 arcconf ssacli hpssacli; do
        [ -f "config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/$t" ] && echo "$t present"
    done

Notes:

* Only the tools actually present are used; detection priority is
  storcli -> perccli -> arcconf -> ssacli -> sg3_utils.
* If only a 64-bit or vendor-branded binary exists, 010-install-app.hook.chroot
  creates a small compat shim (storcli -> storcli64/perccli64/perccli,
  ssacli -> hpssacli) so the unchanged erase command table keeps working.
* With no vendor tool present the image still works in "generic" mode using
  sg3_utils + smartctl + hdparm + nvme-cli, but it can only reach disks that are
  directly visible to the OS (no disks behind a hardware RAID, no RAID
  management).
* Keep the binary names exactly as shown - core/detect.py resolves them through
  PATH and expects those names.
